   "subject": "Re: Using renjin as a sandbox",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<p dir=\"ltr\">Hi Shahar,<br>\r\nSandboxing is one of the use cases around which Renjin was designed. Running untrusted code is always a challenge, and the right solution will depend on the sort of things you want R code to be able to do, but here are some pointers:<br>\r\n1. Provide your own FileSystemManager to control or prohibit access to the physical fs. See [1] for an example.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">2. Evaluate scripts in a seperate thread with a timeout to prevent infinite loops.<br>\r\n3. Use SecurityManager or a library like java-sandbox [2] to prevent R code from doing nasty things like import(java.lang.System)$exit()</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">H<br></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">[1]<a href=\"https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/appengine/src/main/java/org/renjin/appengine/AppEngineContextFactory.java\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/appengine/src/main/java/org/renjin/appengine/AppEngineContextFactory.java&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343946941000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Ivg_9OXbagF5jsGmLH09X\">https://github.com/bedatadriven/renjin/blob/master/appengine/src/main/java/org/renjin/appengine/AppEngineContextFactory.java</a></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">[2]<a href=\"http://blog.datenwerke.net/p/the-java-sandbox.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://blog.datenwerke.net/p/the-java-sandbox.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793343946941000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3TBphcrs14YrvdSZSs1slR\">http://blog.datenwerke.net/p/the-java-sandbox.html</a></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">HTH,<br>\r\nAlex</p>\r\n<div style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi guys,<div>We are considering using renjin for running R scripts through Java, and i&#39;m trying to understand whether i can control the following use cases:</div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18.1818180084229px\">1. stop infinite loops?</span><br style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18.1818180084229px\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Arial,sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:18.1818180084229px\">2. prevent renjin from reading/deleting files?</span><br></div><div><br clear=\"all\"><div>Basically, our requirement is to use renjin as a sandbox so it won&#39;t harm our application that wraps it.</div><div><br></div><div>Will appreciate your quick help,</div><div>Thanks in advance</div>-- <br><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><br style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"color:rgb(136,136,136)\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small\"><font face=\"tahoma, sans-serif\" size=\"1\"><b>Shahar Cohen</b></font></div><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small\"><font face=\"tahoma, sans-serif\" size=\"1\">Software engineer, Research &amp; Development</font></div><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small\"><a href style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204);font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\" data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">sha...@datorama.com</a><span style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\"> </span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\">m: <a value=\"+13475143402\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" rel=\"nofollow\">+972 506.365.142</a> </span></div><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma,sans-serif;font-size:x-small\">s:   shaharc2</span><br></div><div style=\"font-family:ar